A-NAS shows each step of a VNAS turn with a clip of its own: reading a file,
searching, running a command, looking at a photo. Most of these clips are
category actions, outside the stage's pool. dsh-pet's work status carries a
stage and a task line only, and the card picks the stage's clip from its slot.
The work status now also carries the clip the step asks for: the store keeps it
with the task (setDetail writes both at once), the bridge publishes it, the
page's reader keeps it, and the card plays it when the pet has it, the stage's
slot otherwise. It loops while the stage lasts (a clip that ends mid-stage plays
again instead of handing over to the random chain), stops looping when the
stage goes idle, and comes back after a click, a drag or the end of a lock.

